doublecmd.lpi requires LCL >= 3.0. The only 3.0 API used by 1.2.9 is
TSpeedButton.Alignment, already handled by patch 0004, so with Lazarus 2.2.0
the project itself is buildable. Lower the declared minimum to the LCL that
Void ships. (If Void moves to Lazarus 3.x, this patch can go.)

--- a/src/doublecmd.lpi
+++ b/src/doublecmd.lpi
@@ -327,7 +327,7 @@
       </Item8>
       <Item9>
         <PackageName Value="LCL"/>
-        <MinVersion Major="3" Minor="0" Valid="True"/>
+        <MinVersion Major="2" Minor="2" Valid="True"/>
       </Item9>
       <Item10>
         <PackageName Value="SynEdit"/>
